\f0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 I went through the current Scrivener package rather than relying on the old Fridge Force scene. The manuscript gives 
\f1\b TRAMPS and PAPER quite different jobs
\f0\b0 , and your instinct that TRAMPS is the natural first responder to the mansion robberies is strongly supported.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 TRAMPS
\f0\b0  is the ordinary police apparatus of Ulyssia, however grotesquely corporatised and corrupt it has become. The manuscript most often expands it as the 
\f1\b Department of Traffic Movement and Property Security
\f0\b0 ; the Alexander character material explicitly says it was \'93formerly known as the Police.\'94 It has homicide, crime scenes, arrests, evidence, riot squads, patrol/response hover-copts, public relations, and a physical TRAMPS Tower. Hayley is a TRAMPS detective; Alexander is a TRAMPS lieutenant and public face; Gerry Hardman becomes its Commissioner. There is an occasional variant 
\f1\b \'93Traffic Movement and Property Security Incorporated\'94
\f0\b0 , which looks like either a corporatised later name or an unresolved nomenclature variant, but its function is consistently 
\f1\b the police
\f0\b0 .\
The manuscript is particularly explicit about its operational role. Gerry says in the TMinus planning scene:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'93PAPER oversight for intelligence and logistics. TRAMPS for operations.\'94\
That is probably the clearest division of labour anywhere in the book. TRAMPS supplies the people who actually 
\f1\b turn up, investigate, cordon, arrest, raid, control crowds and conduct operations
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 PAPER
\f0\b0 , by contrast, is the 
\f1\b Bureau of Preemptive Reciprocity and Proactive Euthanasia
\f0\b0 . It sits under the 
\f1\b Director of Freedom
\f0\b0 , who is described as keeper of national intelligence. PAPER is repeatedly called clandestine, a secret service, famously lethal and paranoid. Its assets include deep-cover agents, tactical-response teams, armoured hover-copts/gunships, black operations, extensive surveillance/data access, and 
\f1\b Truth Central
\f0\b0 , its secure installation/interrogation complex. Halo is a deep PAPER operative; Agent Jones is PAPER; PAPER embeds moles inside the regular police apparatus. Gerry himself is explicitly a 
\f1\b deep PAPER plant who becomes Commissioner of TRAMPS
\f0\b0 .\
That last fact is particularly useful here because it means you do 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  need to choose between Gerry/TRAMPS and the larger conspiracy machinery. Gerry can respond legitimately 
\f1\b as Commissioner of the police
\f0\b0  to a spectacular string of burglaries, while privately viewing whatever he learns through his PAPER role.\
The robberies themselves sit squarely inside TRAMPS territory. They are multiple break-and-enters into Airborne properties, theft of valuable components from domestic stasis installations, compromised household security systems and presumably identifiable perpetrators convoying around in white Lincolns. 
\f1\b \'93Property Security\'94 is literally in TRAMPS\'92 name.
\f0\b0  Even without anyone understanding what the Gyges discs can do, this is already their case.\
Fridge Force has a different interest. From the rest of the manuscript, it regulates and protects 
\f1\b stasis technology and stasis security
\f0\b0 ; Chip explicitly says Fridge Force does not investigate murders. It can demand information about compromised stasis equipment, recover components, impose technical/regulatory consequences and become extremely unpleasant about unauthorised interference. But nothing I found makes it the natural criminal investigative agency.\
PAPER only becomes the obvious institutional responder once the event is framed as something beyond burglary: 
\f1\b national security, terrorism, clandestine weapons acquisition, a threat to the state, or an intelligence matter
\f0\b0 . That could happen very quickly because the stolen objects are Gyges discs and because Gerry knows considerably more than a normal Commissioner should. But it is an escalation, not the obvious agency receiving seventeen burglar alarms.\
There is also useful confirmation in the 
\f1\b stale \'93Fridge Force learns of the heist\'94 draft itself
\f0\b0 . Despite all its wrong material, Dunhilton summons 
\f1\b Gerry Hardman
\f0\b0 , asks him to identify the Elvi involved, and Gerry asks whether PAPER should be informed. Dunhilton says no. So even that draft's underlying institutional logic was already: 
\f1\b Gerry/the police handle the robbery; PAPER is a separate question requiring escalation.
\f0\b0 \
One other relevant manuscript tension: Alexander complains elsewhere that intelligence agencies, especially PAPER, have been 
\f1\b \'93stepping in on roles that rightfully belong to TRAMPS.\'94
\f0\b0  That establishes jurisdictional rivalry. A spectacular Airborne property crime would therefore be exactly the sort of event TRAMPS would regard as 
\f1\b theirs
\f0\b0 , particularly if PAPER tried to muscle in later.\
So the current institutional picture I\'92d carry forward is:\
